1
00:00:01,559 --> 00:00:03,080
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,800
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,920
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,119
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:10,479
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,879
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,320
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGH]

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,160
Peppa Pig.

9
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,400
[SNORTS]

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,640
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,360
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig
have a new picture

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,799
of Peppa and George.

13
00:00:28,799 --> 00:00:32,600
We should put this lovely
new picture on the wall.

14
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,360
Leave it to me.

15
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,879
I am the DIY expert
of the house.

16
00:00:36,879 --> 00:00:38,920
Are you sure
you can do it?

17
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:40,120
Of course.

18
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,760
I'll just put
a nail in the wall

19
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,480
and hang the picture
on it.

20
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:46,919
Very good. I'm just off to visit
Granny and Grandpa Pig.

21
00:00:46,919 --> 00:00:49,519
I'll see you later.

22
00:00:49,519 --> 00:00:50,760
[ENGINE STARTS]

23
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:52,800
And please
don't make a mess.

24
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,599
[LAUGHS]
Mess?

25
00:00:54,599 --> 00:00:56,080
Goodbye.

26
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,960
[CAR HORN HONKS]
ALL: Goodbye.

27
00:00:59,199 --> 00:01:00,720
[LAUGHS]

28
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:02,959
Daddy, can we help
put up the picture?

29
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:07,399
You can watch, and then you'll
learn how to do it properly.

30
00:01:07,399 --> 00:01:10,320
First, I need
a tape measure.

31
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,200
And a pencil.

32
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,160
[SNORTS]

33
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,240
That is where
I'm going to put the nail.

34
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:24,000
Don't break the wall,
Daddy.

35
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,360
[LAUGHS]

36
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:28,720
DADDY PIG:
Now I need a hammer and a nail.

37
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:32,240
Stand back, children,
and watch a craftsman at work.

38
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:35,080
Daddy Pig is going to knock
the nail into the wall.

39
00:01:36,399 --> 00:01:37,479
[SNORTS]

40
00:01:37,479 --> 00:01:39,440
Don't break the wall,
Daddy.

41
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:41,920
[LAUGHS]
Don't be silly, Peppa.

42
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,560
[SNORTS]

43
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,920
Easy as pie.

44
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:49,320
Oh, it's not meant
to do that.

45
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,399
Daddy Pig has made
a big crack in the wall.

46
00:01:52,399 --> 00:01:55,679
Oh, Daddy.
You've broken the wall.

47
00:01:55,679 --> 00:01:59,479
It's just a tiny crack.
The picture will hide it.

48
00:01:59,479 --> 00:02:01,280
There.

49
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,880
I can still see
the crack, Daddy.

50
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:07,880
Yes, I'll just take the nail out
and fill in the crack.

51
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,759
Don't make a mess, Daddy.

52
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,920
[LAUGHS]
Don't be silly, Peppa.

53
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,480
[GRUNTS]

54
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,280
It's coming out.

55
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,600
Whoa!

56
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,000
Oh, Daddy.

57
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,840
Now you really
have broken the wall.

58
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,079
Hmm.

59
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:27,440
Do you think Mommy
will notice?

60
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,200
Uh, yes, I think
she might.

61
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,840
[BOTH LAUGH]

62
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,959
Quick, George.

63
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,760
What are they doing?

64
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,000
[SNORTING]

65
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,560
Daddy, we can see you.

66
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,959
[BOTH LAUGH]

67
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:43,200
Hmm.

68
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,799
Daddy Pig
has to mend the wall

69
00:02:44,799 --> 00:02:46,560
before Mommy Pig
comes home.

70
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,440
DADDY PIG:
Brick, please.

71
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:54,239
First, Daddy Pig fills the hole
with bricks.

72
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,440
[BOTH LAUGH]

73
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:05,920
[SNORTS]

74
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:08,359
There.
[BOTH SNICKER]

75
00:03:08,359 --> 00:03:11,959
Next, Daddy Pig puts plaster
over the bricks.

76
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,799
[LAUGHS]

77
00:03:15,799 --> 00:03:17,399
Easy as pie.

78
00:03:17,399 --> 00:03:19,959
Then Daddy Pig
paints the wall.

79
00:03:22,359 --> 00:03:25,079
[BOTH LAUGHING]

80
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,760
[SNORTS]
Good as new.

81
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,280
The wall is mended.

82
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:31,679
Hooray!
[BOTH LAUGH]

83
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:33,799
But look at all the mess
they have made.

84
00:03:33,799 --> 00:03:35,160
Goodness me.

85
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,679
We had better clean up
before Mommy comes back.

86
00:03:37,679 --> 00:03:41,040
First, Daddy pig quickly washes
Peppa and George.

87
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:44,600
Then Peppa
vacuums the floor.

88
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,239
And Daddy Pig
tidies up the tools.

89
00:03:47,239 --> 00:03:48,519
[CAR HORN HONKS]

90
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:50,040
[GASPS]
Mommy.

91
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,760
Mommy Pig is home.

92
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,359
[CAR HORN HONKS]

93
00:03:53,359 --> 00:03:54,519
Mommy!

94
00:03:54,519 --> 00:03:55,959
[GASPS]
Mommy's here.

95
00:03:55,959 --> 00:03:58,560
Quick, pretend nothing
has happened.

96
00:04:00,079 --> 00:04:01,560
[SNORTS]
Hello.

97
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,880
Hello.
[LAUGHS NERVOUSLY]

98
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,880
What have you been doing?

99
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,320
Oh, nothing.

100
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,399
[BOTH GIGGLING]

101
00:04:09,399 --> 00:04:12,480
Yes, I can see
you've been doing nothing.

102
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:15,280
I thought you were going
to put the picture up.

103
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,839
In all the excitement,
Daddy Pig has forgotten

104
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:19,039
to put the picture up.

105
00:04:19,039 --> 00:04:20,320
Oh.

106
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,959
Well, I'm no expert,

107
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:24,280
but I'm sure
it's quite easy.

108
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:28,360
[SNORTS]
There.

109
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:32,080
Hmm, yes, that did look
quite easy.

110
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:35,159
But when you did it, Daddy,,
it looked really hard.

111
00:04:35,159 --> 00:04:37,760
Shush, Peppa.
Don't tell anyone.

112
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,880
[ALL LAUGH]

113
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,320
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

114
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:54,440
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family
are going to the beach.

115
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,919
Peppa and George
love going to the beach.

116
00:04:56,919 --> 00:04:58,560
[BOTH LAUGHING]

117
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,560
What a lot of stuff.

118
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:08,360
We must be careful not to forget
anything when we go.

119
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,440
Sunshade, beach bag,
towels,

120
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:15,200
buckets and spades,
and a spotty ball.

121
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,120
Good. Now, before you start
playing,

122
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,080
you need some
sun cream on you.

123
00:05:21,599 --> 00:05:23,440
The sun is very hot,

124
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:26,360
so Peppa and George
have to have sun cream on.

125
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,520
Let's try out
this spotty ball.

126
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,960
It seems to work.

127
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,159
[CHUCKLES]

128
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:33,840
What a great spotty ball.

129
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,960
[BOTH LAUGH]

130
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:42,919
George, you throw the ball,
and I will catch it.

131
00:05:42,919 --> 00:05:44,599
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

132
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,200
George, catch.

133
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:51,039
Oh, dear. George is too little
to catch the ball.

134
00:05:51,039 --> 00:05:52,599
[CRIES]

135
00:05:53,919 --> 00:05:55,400
Never mind, George.

136
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:58,039
Would you and Peppa like to have
a paddle in the sea?

137
00:05:58,039 --> 00:06:00,280
Yes, please, Daddy.
[SNORTING]

138
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,760
Let's put your water wings on.

139
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,719
[BLOWING]

140
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,599
There we go.

141
00:06:09,599 --> 00:06:12,240
You look very smart
in your water wings, George.

142
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,479
[LAUGHS]

143
00:06:13,479 --> 00:06:15,280
My turn. My turn.

144
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,000
[BLOWS]

145
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,000
Good.

146
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,159
[LAUGHS]

147
00:06:21,159 --> 00:06:22,799
Now we can play
in the Water.

148
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,039
Hooray!

149
00:06:24,039 --> 00:06:25,680
[BOTH GIGGLE]

150
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,200
[SNORTS]

151
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,320
Is the water cold?

152
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:33,039
It's lovely
and warm.

153
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:34,320
Aah!

154
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:36,080
[LAUGHS]

155
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:38,240
[LAUGHS]

156
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,000
[ALL LAUGHING]

157
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,080
Steady on.

158
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:46,440
You started it,
Daddy Pig.

159
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,880
Maybe that's enough
splashing.

160
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,120
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

161
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,440
Whee!

162
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:57,159
Daddy, I love being
at the beach.

163
00:06:57,159 --> 00:06:59,120
Peppa and George
love the beach.

164
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,880
Everyone loves the beach.

165
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,440
MOMMY PIG:
Peppa, George.

166
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:05,320
Would you like to play
with your buckets and spades?

167
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,640
Yes, please, Mommy.

168
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:11,919
Daddy. Daddy.

169
00:07:11,919 --> 00:07:14,239
Can we bury you
in the sand?

170
00:07:14,239 --> 00:07:15,680
Uh, well...

171
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,640
Please, Daddy.

172
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,640
Oh, all right.

173
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,680
Yippee!
[SNORTS]

174
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,799
[ALL LAUGH]

175
00:07:25,479 --> 00:07:29,000
Peppa and George are burying
Daddy Pig in the sand.

176
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,640
Steady on.

177
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,440
[ALL LAUGH]

178
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,680
There.

179
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,520
Now you can't escape.

180
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,919
My head is getting
a bit hot.

181
00:07:37,919 --> 00:07:39,479
Can I have
my straw hat?

182
00:07:39,479 --> 00:07:42,239
Well, if you say "please."

183
00:07:42,239 --> 00:07:44,520
Please can I have
my straw hat?

184
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:46,239
Yes, you may, Daddy.

185
00:07:46,239 --> 00:07:48,560
[GIGGLES]

186
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,760
[SNORTS]

187
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,039
That's nice.

188
00:07:51,039 --> 00:07:52,599
[YAWNS]

189
00:07:52,599 --> 00:07:55,400
Maybe I'll just have
a little sleep.

190
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,280
[SNORES]

191
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,520
[BOTH LAUGH]

192
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,400
George, let's make
sand castles.

193
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,719
Peppa and George
are making sand castles.

194
00:08:05,719 --> 00:08:07,840
First we put sand
in the buckets.

195
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,719
Like this.

196
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:15,640
We turn the buckets upside down
and tap them.

197
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:17,520
And lift the bucket up.

198
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,479
Hey, presto.

199
00:08:19,479 --> 00:08:20,799
A sand castle.

200
00:08:20,799 --> 00:08:22,799
[SNORTS]
Hey, presto.

201
00:08:22,799 --> 00:08:24,760
Another sand castle.

202
00:08:25,799 --> 00:08:27,520
MOMMY PIG:
Peppa, George.

203
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:28,719
Home time.

204
00:08:28,719 --> 00:08:30,520
Don't leave
any stuff behind.

205
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:31,960
[BOTH LAUGH]

206
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:34,600
Let's check that we haven't
forgotten anything.

207
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,400
Towels, beach bag,

208
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:39,000
sunshade,
and the spotty ball.

209
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,319
That's everything.

210
00:08:40,319 --> 00:08:42,600
I'm sure we've forgotten
something.

211
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:44,560
Hmm.
[SNORTS]

212
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,880
[LAUGHS]

213
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,640
Of course.

214
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,840
We forgot the hat.
[SNORTS]

215
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,280
[SNORING]

216
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,640
PEPPA:
Daddy!

217
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,199
We forgot Daddy!

218
00:08:56,199 --> 00:08:59,160
Oh, yes!
We forgot Daddy Pig.

219
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,240
Huh? What?

220
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,680
Daddy, we almost
left you behind.

221
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,680
But George remembered you.

222
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,000
[SNORTS]
[LAUGHS]

223
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,800
Well, I'm glad
George remembered me.

224
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,520
[ALL LAUGH]

225
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:24,720
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

226
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:27,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa is playing
with her doll's house.

227
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:28,959
George is playing too.

228
00:09:28,959 --> 00:09:30,480
[BOTH LAUGH]

229
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,920
Peppa making a tea party
for the doll family.

230
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,520
[SNORTS]
Here, George.

231
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:37,959
I'm the mommy and daddy.
You can be the children.

232
00:09:37,959 --> 00:09:39,199
[LAUGHS]

233
00:09:39,199 --> 00:09:40,720
[SNORTS]
Children.

234
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:44,360
It's nearly tea time,
so you must wash your hands.

235
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:46,480
[SNORTING]

236
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:49,360
George is putting
the dolls to bed.

237
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,040
Night night.

238
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,280
George, why are you putting
the children to bed?

239
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:56,480
They're having
a tea party.

240
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:59,400
George likes putting
the dolls to bed.

241
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:05,120
Children, come down stairs right
now or you won't get any cake.

242
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,600
George isn't listening.

243
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,959
He's too busy
putting the dolls to bed.

244
00:10:08,959 --> 00:10:12,480
George, if you want to play
with my doll's house,

245
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,959
you have to help
with the tea party.

246
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,400
Here, George, you can fill
the teapot with water.

247
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,720
[SNORTS]

248
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,760
Children, come downstairs
right now.

249
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,720
Mommy, we're coming.

250
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:30,000
[LAUGHS]

251
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,040
George is going to fill
the teapot with water.

252
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,160
Ooh.

253
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,640
George has found a spider
in the sink.

254
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,040
[LAUGHS]

255
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:43,480
George wants the spider
to be his friend.

256
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,240
Oh.

257
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,959
[GIGGLES]

258
00:10:48,959 --> 00:10:51,000
George likes the spider.

259
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
The spider likes George.

260
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,280
[LAUGHS]

261
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,600
Peppa loves playing
tea parties.

262
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,920
[LAUGHING]

263
00:10:57,920 --> 00:11:00,680
Where are all the chocolate
biscuits, Daddy?

264
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:03,319
We had lots yesterday.

265
00:11:03,319 --> 00:11:07,240
Oh, I'm sorry, Mommy.
I must have eaten them all.

266
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,000
Ho, ho, ho.

267
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,240
[LAUGHS]

268
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,719
Naughty daddy.

269
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,680
George is putting
the spider to bed.

270
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,280
Night night.

271
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,640
George, what are you doing?

272
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,199
You have to help me
with the tea party.

273
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,920
[SCREAMS]

274
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:32,120
Help! Help!

275
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:35,240
Daddy! There's a spider
in my bedroom!

276
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,560
Oh, don't worry, Peppa.

277
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:40,680
Please, Daddy,
take it away.

278
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,079
[LAUGHING]

279
00:11:42,079 --> 00:11:44,439
No need to panic.

280
00:11:44,439 --> 00:11:47,160
Hello, George.
Have you seen the spider?

281
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:48,360
[SNORTS]

282
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:50,040
It's too scary.

283
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,560
Take it away.

284
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:53,880
There's no need
to be afraid, Peppa.

285
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,000
[SNORTS]

286
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,839
Spiders are very,
very small,

287
00:11:56,839 --> 00:11:58,480
and they can't hurt you.

288
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,959
But don't worry.

289
00:11:59,959 --> 00:12:02,360
Daddy will take it
out of the bedroom.

290
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,079
Whoa!

291
00:12:04,079 --> 00:12:06,560
He's quite big,
isn't he?

292
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:09,079
Um, I'll just fetch
Mommy Pig.

293
00:12:09,079 --> 00:12:10,680
Mommy Pig!

294
00:12:12,719 --> 00:12:14,160
[LAUGHS]

295
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,839
Hello, Mr. Skinnylegs.

296
00:12:15,839 --> 00:12:18,079
Peppa feels
a little bit braver.

297
00:12:18,079 --> 00:12:20,640
He likes being
in my doll's house.

298
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:24,199
Hello, children, I hear
you've found a little spider.

299
00:12:24,199 --> 00:12:27,439
I'll take him out the bedroom
so you two can play.

300
00:12:27,439 --> 00:12:31,600
Mommy, his name
is Mr. Skinnylegs.

301
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:35,599
Aah! Mr. Skinnylegs
is big, isn't he?

302
00:12:35,599 --> 00:12:37,000
[PEPPA AND GEORGE GIGGLE]

303
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,280
Peppa and George
like the spider.

304
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,520
[SNORTING]

305
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,839
Night night.

306
00:12:42,839 --> 00:12:44,920
George is putting
the spider to bed.

307
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,160
No, George!

308
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,640
He wants some tea.

309
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:50,120
He doesn't want
to be in bed.

310
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:53,079
Are you hungry,
Mr. Skinnylegs?

311
00:12:53,079 --> 00:12:54,719
Would you like some cake?

312
00:12:54,719 --> 00:12:57,640
Peppa isn't afraid
of the spider anymore.

313
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:00,199
Mommy, Daddy, sit down.

314
00:13:00,199 --> 00:13:04,599
We are all going to have tea
with Mr. Skinnylegs.

315
00:13:04,599 --> 00:13:06,599
[SNORTS]
Who wants tea?

316
00:13:06,599 --> 00:13:08,040
Me, please.
Me, please.

317
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,319
[SNORTS]

318
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,920
Delicious.

319
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:15,199
Peppa loves playing
tea parties.

320
00:13:15,199 --> 00:13:18,120
[LAUGHS]
Here's your tea, Mr. Skinnylegs.

321
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,000
What's that?

322
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,680
You want to say hello
to my daddy?

323
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:25,160
Hello, Mr. Daddy Pig.

324
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,719
Uh, that's all right, Peppa.

325
00:13:27,719 --> 00:13:30,000
Let Mr. Skinnylegs
drink his tea.

326
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,240
You're not scared,
are you, Daddy?

327
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:34,400
Oh, no, of course not.

328
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,880
Aah! Not so close.

329
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,839
[LAUGHS]
Whoa!

330
00:13:38,839 --> 00:13:40,160
[GASPS]

331
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:41,880
[ALL LAUGH]

332
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,839
Peppa likes Mr. Skinnylegs.

333
00:13:43,839 --> 00:13:46,920
Everyone likes
Mr. Skinnylegs.

334
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:53,719
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

335
00:13:53,719 --> 00:13:57,599
NARRATOR:
Granny Pig and Grandpa Pig
are taking Peppa and George out

336
00:13:57,599 --> 00:13:58,760
for a day on the river.

337
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,040
Welcome aboard,
me hearties.

338
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:02,560
[SNORTS]
Peppa, George.

339
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:05,199
Let's put
your life jackets on.

340
00:14:05,199 --> 00:14:07,880
When Peppa and George
are on Grandpa Pig's boat,

341
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,640
they must wear life jackets.

342
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:13,160
On this boat,
I'm the captain.

343
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:14,439
Aye, aye, captain.

344
00:14:14,439 --> 00:14:16,319
Aye, aye, captain.
[SNORTS]

345
00:14:16,319 --> 00:14:19,719
When Captain Grandpa
tells you all to do something,

346
00:14:19,719 --> 00:14:21,839
you must do it.

347
00:14:21,839 --> 00:14:24,280
[WHISPERING]
Unless it's something silly.

348
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,400
Captain Grandpa
never says anything silly.

349
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,640
Of course not,
Captain Grandpa.

350
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,120
[BOTH GIGGLE]

351
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,680
George, raise the flag.

352
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,120
[SNORTING]

353
00:14:36,599 --> 00:14:39,400
Peppa, ring the bell.

354
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,719
Aye, aye, captain.
[CLANGING]

355
00:14:41,719 --> 00:14:44,439
Granny Pig,
take the wheel.

356
00:14:44,439 --> 00:14:46,240
Aye, aye, captain.

357
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,240
Full sail.

358
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,280
[MOTOR REVS]

359
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:51,520
Full sail.

360
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,760
[SNORTS]

361
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,199
[BOTH LAUGH]

362
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,520
[QUACKING]

363
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,240
Maybe you should go
a little slower, Grandpa Pig.

364
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:03,439
Good idea, Granny Pig.

365
00:15:03,439 --> 00:15:06,479
I don't want to use up
all my petrol.

366
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:11,520
Grandpa, I liked it
when we went fast.

367
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:15,160
Don't worry, Peppa,
we'll go fast later.

368
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,479
[SNORTS]
Look!

369
00:15:16,479 --> 00:15:18,000
There's another boat.

370
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,719
Here's Granddad Dog.

371
00:15:19,719 --> 00:15:22,280
He's taking Danny Dog out
for a day on the river.

372
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:24,880
Ahoy there,
Granddad Dog!

373
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,800
Ahoy there,
Grandpa Pig!

374
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:29,479
Hello, Danny.
[BELL CLANGS]

375
00:15:29,479 --> 00:15:31,319
Hello, Peppa.
[HORN TOOTS]

376
00:15:31,319 --> 00:15:33,360
[BOTH LAUGH]

377
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:36,599
Granddad Dog is Grandpa Pig's
very best friend.

378
00:15:36,599 --> 00:15:38,199
[LAUGHS]

379
00:15:38,199 --> 00:15:42,360
I'm surprised your boat
is still afloat, Granddad Dog.

380
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,520
It must be almost as old
as you are.

381
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,719
[BARKS]

382
00:15:45,719 --> 00:15:47,880
This old boat
can go faster

383
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:51,000
than your rusty bucket
any day, Grandpa Pig.

384
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,400
All right, you old sea dog,
race you.

385
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,240
Prepare to lose,
water hog.

386
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:00,359
[SNORTING]
[BARKING]

387
00:16:00,359 --> 00:16:03,280
You two are acting like
little children.

388
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,599
[BOTH LAUGH]

389
00:16:04,599 --> 00:16:07,520
Granddad Dog called me
a water hog.

390
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:10,640
You called him a sea dog first,
Grandpa.

391
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:12,640
You should say sorry.

392
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:15,520
Only if he says
sorry first.

393
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:18,839
Granddad, say sorry
to Grandpa Pig.

394
00:16:18,839 --> 00:16:20,359
He is your best friend.

395
00:16:20,359 --> 00:16:25,120
No. He's a water hog,
and my boat is faster than his.

396
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,319
All right, sea dog.

397
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,560
Let's race
to the next bridge.

398
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:32,280
On the count of three!

399
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,319
One, two...

400
00:16:34,319 --> 00:16:36,000
Go!

401
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,640
You started too soon.

402
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:41,280
Catch me if you can,
water hog!

403
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,520
[BARKS]

404
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:43,839
Sea dog!

405
00:16:43,839 --> 00:16:45,240
[SNORTS]

406
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:50,640
Is that as fast
as you can go?

407
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,839
[SNORTS]

408
00:16:51,839 --> 00:16:53,160
Can't catch me!

409
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:54,439
[LAUGHS]

410
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,240
I win!

411
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,760
[ENGINE SPUTTERS]

412
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,199
Oh, dear.

413
00:17:00,199 --> 00:17:02,959
Grandpa Pig's boat
has run out of petrol.

414
00:17:02,959 --> 00:17:05,000
Very clever,
Captain Grandpa.

415
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,520
Maybe I did go
a bit too fast.

416
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:09,839
How will we get home?

417
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:11,919
Look, there's Granddad Dog.

418
00:17:11,919 --> 00:17:14,040
[HORN TOOTS]

419
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:16,319
Granddad Dog
can tow us home.

420
00:17:16,319 --> 00:17:19,839
I'm not being towed
by that sea dog.

421
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:22,760
I haven't offered
to tow the water hog.

422
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,960
[SIGHS]

423
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,040
Will you two
ever grow up?

424
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:29,520
Grandpa, say sorry
to Granddad Dog.

425
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:34,040
I'm sorry I called you
a sea dog.

426
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:37,320
Granddad, say sorry
to Grandpa Pig.

427
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:40,720
I'm sorry I called you
a water hog.

428
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:42,280
That's nice.

429
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:46,639
Granddad Dog, would you be
so kind as to tow us home?

430
00:17:46,639 --> 00:17:49,240
It would be my pleasure, madame!

431
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,800
Catch this, captain.

432
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,840
Aye, aye, skipper.

433
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:56,080
Granddad Dog is Grandpa Pig's
very best friend.

434
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,680
[SNORTS]
[BARKS]

435
00:17:57,680 --> 00:18:01,040
Granddad Dog is towing
Grandpa Pig's boat home.

436
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:05,240
The main thing is,
I won the race.

437
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,680
Grandpa Pig!

438
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,840
Naughty Grandpa Pig.

439
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,360
[ALL LAUGH]

440
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,520
Peppa, ring the bell.

441
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,360
Aye, aye,
Captain Grandpa.

442
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,600
[BELL CLANGS]

443
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,240
[HORN TOOTS]

444
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,680
[PEPPA LAUGHING AND SNORTING]

445
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,040
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

446
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:26,560
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

447
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,600
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

448
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,800
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

449
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:32,960
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

450
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,760
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

